<title>ITALY: Italy rail groups to join forces in China.</title>
<headline>Italy rail groups to join forces in China.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The engineering arm of the Italian state railway company said on Thursday it was joining forces with four other railway engineering groups to supply turnkey railway systems for the Chinese market.</p>
<p>The group, Italferr-sis T.A.V., said it had reached a preliminary accord with Ansaldo Trasporti, Breda Ferroviaria, Fiat Ferroviaria and Sasib Railway. It gave no further details of the systems to be supplied.</p>
<p>Italy's state-owned Ferrovie dello Stato railway company signed a cooperation agreement in 1996 with the Chinese government.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
